1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:02,395
An agent can move money in seconds.

2
00:00:02,395 --> 00:00:05,501
The harder question is whether the work was actually done.

3
00:00:05,501 --> 00:00:10,759
Tranche turns a milestone into a test the agent has to pass before it
gets paid.

4
00:00:11,370 --> 00:00:14,515
The useful part of a payment demo is the refusal.

5
00:00:14,515 --> 00:00:18,844
A claim can look finished while the demo link is dead or the numbers
are made up.

6
00:00:18,844 --> 00:00:21,460
Someone has to check before the money leaves.

7
00:00:22,089 --> 00:00:26,009
The release room lists every milestone and every decision.

8
00:00:26,009 --> 00:00:27,658
Two bounties were blocked.

9
00:00:27,658 --> 00:00:29,126
Two releases settled.

10
00:00:29,126 --> 00:00:32,490
The small one settled through Kite Passport, on Base.

11
00:00:33,129 --> 00:00:35,140
Here is a milestone that passed.

12
00:00:35,140 --> 00:00:40,772
The repository is public, the demo responds, and the claim matches the
links.

13
00:00:40,772 --> 00:00:42,292
SERV reads the claim.

14
00:00:42,292 --> 00:00:44,676
Reppo evaluates it independently.

15
00:00:44,676 --> 00:00:47,899
Both accept, and the policy releases the tranche.

16
00:00:48,509 --> 00:00:49,838
This is the settlement.

17
00:00:49,838 --> 00:00:52,801
Ten cents, real money, on Base.

18
00:00:52,801 --> 00:00:57,054
The receipt shows the rail, the amount, and the transaction hash.

19
00:00:57,054 --> 00:01:03,871
The payout was created by the app, approved with a passkey, and
recorded only after the signed send came back.

20
00:01:04,489 --> 00:01:05,664
Now the refusal.

21
00:01:05,664 --> 00:01:09,039
This claim says the demo works and the numbers are real.

22
00:01:09,039 --> 00:01:11,359
The link returns a 404.

23
00:01:11,359 --> 00:01:13,266
The numbers are not in the README.

24
00:01:13,266 --> 00:01:14,581
SERV rejects it.

25
00:01:14,581 --> 00:01:16,152
Reppo rejects it too.

26
00:01:16,152 --> 00:01:19,323
Zero dollars moved, and the receipt says why.

27
00:01:19,939 --> 00:01:21,989
The policy also has a ceiling.

28
00:01:21,989 --> 00:01:25,418
This tranche is five hundred dollars, above the limit.

29
00:01:25,418 --> 00:01:28,909
Even with a passing verdict, the payment waits for a human.

30
00:01:28,909 --> 00:01:31,706
The model never gets to move money on its own.

31
00:01:32,340 --> 00:01:35,524
Tranche is the acceptance layer for agent payments.

32
00:01:35,524 --> 00:01:36,877
The agent can pay.

33
00:01:36,877 --> 00:01:38,875
The proof decides whether it should.

34
00:01:38,875 --> 00:01:40,163
Pay when it's proven.

